## Definition

HTTP is a protocol used to transfer web pages between a web browser and a web server.

## Port

80

## Purpose

Used to access websites on the Internet.

## Example

When you open:

http://example.com

your browser sends an HTTP request to the web server, and the server sends the webpage back.

## Security

Data is not encrypted.

## SOC Perspective

If a login page uses HTTP instead of HTTPS, an attacker can capture usernames and passwords using packet sniffing.

